# =============================================================================
# BallKnower Gridiron — .gitignore
#
# The governing rule: everything regenerable stays out, everything that is
# EVIDENCE goes in. The forecast ledger under content/football/ is the whole
# point of the repo being public — it is a timestamped, third-party-attested
# record. It must never be ignored, so there are explicit un-ignore rules for
# it at the bottom.
# =============================================================================

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST

# --- Virtual environments ----------------------------------------------------
venv/
env/
ENV/
.venv/
.env/
env.bak/
venv.bak/

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# .env holds API keys (ESPN/QBR endpoints, any odds provider). Never commit it.
# Commit .env.example instead so a fresh clone knows which vars to set.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.key
secrets.json
credentials.json

# --- Data caches (large, regenerable) ----------------------------------------
# The PBP parquet cache is ~13 seasons x ~50k plays x ~370 columns. That is
# hundreds of megabytes and would blow past GitHub's file-size limits, and it
# re-downloads from nflverse on demand anyway.
data_cache/
!data_cache/.gitkeep
*.parquet
*.feather

# Cached nflverse schedule CSVs — regenerable in seconds.
nfl_schedule_*.csv

# --- Trained model artifacts (large, regenerable, and pickles) ---------------
# Deliberately ignored rather than committed. Pickles are version-fragile
# (a scikit-learn or xgboost upgrade can make them unloadable) and they are
# reproducible from `train_football_model.py` given the same data and settings.
# What actually pins a forecast to a model is `config_hash` + `code_commit`
# in the ledger rows, not the binary itself.
models_artifacts/
!models_artifacts/.gitkeep
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.joblib

# --- Logs and diagnostics ----------------------------------------------------
logs/
!logs/.gitkeep
*.log
# Diagnostic plots and audit dumps are re-derivable from a retrain.
*.png
v5_audit.csv
blend_sweep*.csv

# --- Notebooks ---------------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.ipynb_checkpoints

# --- OS / editor -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- Streamlit ---------------------------------------------------------------
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# =============================================================================
# THE LEDGER — explicitly NOT ignored
#
# `*.png` and the cache rules above could otherwise sweep up files under
# content/. These negations make the published record un-ignorable by accident.
# If a future rule ever shadows one of these, the ledger silently stops being
# committed and the track record quietly develops a hole — which is exactly the
# failure the ledger exists to make impossible.
# =============================================================================
!content/
!content/**
!content/football/**/ledger/
!content/football/**/ledger/forecasts.jsonl
!content/football/**/ledger/manifest.json
!content/football/**/newsletter.md
!content/football/**/newsletter.html
!content/football/**/blog.md
!content/football/**/blog.html
!content/football/**/predictions.json

# Sibling BallKnower packages that have their own git repos.
# Nested repos get staged as gitlinks (mode 160000) — a bare commit SHA that
# clones can't resolve, so the directory would appear empty to anyone who
# cloned this repo. Excluded rather than made a submodule: these are separate
# projects that happen to share a parent folder, not dependencies of this one.
ballknower_fantasy/
